ORIGINAL AUTHOR AND METHOD

The original Photo Material Intervention workflow and its first three recipes
(Portal Woodcut, Paint-Stop Charcoal, and Sunlight Screenprint) were authored
and first publicly released by Pilipala9919 in 2026.

The method's identifying sequence is:

1. diagnose the photographic subject and identity anchors;
2. remove genuine obstructions in a separate documentary stage when needed;
3. derive one dominant handmade-medium event from a boundary already present
   in the source photograph;
4. preserve a truthful photographic anchor;
5. evaluate one-second mobile readability, source specificity, fidelity, and
   physically motivated motion.

